    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i feel like everything i ever made was just a lie. i look at my studio and it just feels like a graveyard of things that don't matter anymore. there's nothing left in me. no more colors, no more ideas... just this massive, empty silence. it feels like i've already finished my story and i'm just waiting for the credits to roll.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear the weight of that emptiness, and it's a heavy thing to carry—like your creative well has run dry and the echoes feel hollow. But a graveyard isn't the end; it's where seeds wait for the right season to break through. The silence isn't proof that you're finished—it's the room you need to relearn what you actually want to say. When you're ready, start with the smallest, most useless mark you can make, not for an audience, just for your own hand. Your story isn't over; you're just between chapters.",
      "source": "target",
